<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- Written by Diver's release workflow on every release; an edit here is
     overwritten by the next one. -->
<package xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/packaging/2015/06/nuspec.xsd">
  <metadata>
    <id>diver</id>
    <version>1.0.0.333</version>
    <packageSourceUrl>https://github.com/SaaS-To-Bentley/homebrew-diver/tree/main/chocolatey</packageSourceUrl>
    <owners>Diver</owners>
    <title>Diver</title>
    <authors>Diver</authors>
    <projectUrl>https://usediver.com/</projectUrl>
    <iconUrl>https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/SaaS-To-Bentley/homebrew-diver@main/icon.svg</iconUrl>
    <requireLicenseAcceptance>false</requireLicenseAcceptance>
    <tags>diver deeplinks deep-links uri adb android developer-tools</tags>
    <summary>Build, launch and document deeplinks.</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[Diver builds a URI from its parts, sends it to a phone, an emulator or the desktop itself, and keeps a history of what opened.

- **Build** a URI as text or as scheme, host, path and query parameters, kept in sync both ways.
- **Send** it to an Android device or emulator over `adb`, to another Diver on the network, or to any device on your Diver account.
- **Keep** the deeplinks your apps support, per organization and environment, and check that their hosted link files are in place.

Diver can download Android's platform-tools for you if `adb` is not installed.
]]></description>
    <releaseNotes>https://github.com/SaaS-To-Bentley/homebrew-diver/releases/tag/v1.0.0-333</releaseNotes>
  </metadata>
  <files>
    <file src="tools\**" target="tools" />
  </files>
</package>
